    'models.fact.size': 'Size',
    'models.fact.download': 'Download',
    'models.fact.about': 'about {gb} GB',
    'models.arch.moe': '{total}B, {active}B active per word (mixture of experts)',
    'models.arch.dense': '{total}B dense',
    'models.arch.gemma4-e4b': 'about 4B, built for laptops and phones',
    'models.why.qwen3.6-35b': 'The all-rounder for 32 GB and up. Only a small part of it works on each word, so it is quick even where memory is slow, and it reads images and video frames.',
    'models.why.qwen3.6-27b': 'Smarter for its size than the 35B-A3B, but every part works on every word, so it is slower. Best on a Mac with a Max or Ultra chip, whose memory is fast.',
    'models.why.gemma4-26b': 'Google\'s quick model with vision: a good second opinion to Qwen at the same size.',
    'models.why.gemma4-31b': 'Google\'s largest Gemma, with vision. Slower than the 26B-A4B, a little more careful.',
    'models.why.gemma4-12b': 'The largest Gemma 4 that fits a 12 or 16 GB graphics card with room for a long conversation, and it sees images. Still a small model: expect to steer it in longer tasks.',
    'models.why.gemma4-e4b': 'Fits a 16 GB Mac or a 12 GB graphics card and sees images. Small models miss steps in longer tasks, so expect to steer it.',
    'models.why.gpt-oss-20b': 'Reliable with tools for its size, and fits 24 GB. Text only.',
    'models.why.gpt-oss-120b': 'The proven pick for 128 GB machines: steady with tools, and around 50 words a second on a DGX Spark or a Ryzen AI Max. Text only.',
    'models.why.qwen3.5-122b': 'The biggest model with vision that fits one 128 GB machine. Smarter than the 35B models, at about half their speed (some 40 words a second on a DGX Spark with vLLM).',
    'models.why.mistral-small-4': 'Apache 2.0, with vision and a switch for how hard it thinks. A strong alternative to Qwen3.5 122B on 128 GB.',
    'models.why.deepseek-v4-flash': 'The model Cedar is built around. Too big for one Spark (about 160 GB); two linked Sparks serve it with vLLM.',
    'models.why.nemotron-3.5-super-vl': 'NVIDIA\'s newest large open model for agents, and it sees images. Fits one Spark (the NVFP4 build is about 75 GB), careful with tools and long tasks, with a switch for how hard it thinks. Text and images.',
    'models.why.nemotron-3.5-lightning': 'NVIDIA\'s quick one, built for agents: only about 3B of it works on each word, so it answers several times faster than Super. Text only.',
    'models.why.qwen3.5-4b': 'Fits the Jetson\'s 8 GB on the GPU, calls tools and reads images. Small models miss steps in longer tasks, so keep requests short and steer it.',
    'models.hosted.deepseek-v4.1-flash': 'Fast, cheap, a million-token memory, and it sees images natively. The best place to start.',
    'models.hosted.glm-5.3': 'One of the strongest open models at multi-step agent work. Use it for text.',
    'models.hosted.kimi-k2.6': 'A trillion-parameter model with vision, good at long tasks. Check which providers list it.',
    'models.hosted.deepseek-v4-pro': 'Flash\'s bigger sibling, for the hardest tasks. Slower and pricier.',
    'models.hosted.qwen3.6-35b-hosted': 'The cheapest model with vision here, the same one you could later run yourself on 32 GB.',
    'models.hosted.gemma4-31b-hosted': 'Google\'s largest Gemma, with vision.',
    'models.servedBy': 'Served by {at}.',
    'models.shell.modelMachine': 'On the model\'s machine',
    'models.get.llamaFirst': 'downloads the model the first time, then serves it on port 8080',
    'models.get.lms': '<strong>LM Studio:</strong> in <em>Discover</em>, search for <code>{name}</code>.',
    'models.get.lmsMac': '<strong>LM Studio:</strong> in <em>Discover</em>, search for <code>{name}</code> and prefer the MLX build.',
    'models.get.vllm': '<strong>vLLM</strong> (fastest on a Spark): serve {what} with tool calling on{flags}; the <a href="{recipe}">vLLM recipes</a> list the flags, and NVIDIA\'s <a href="https://build.nvidia.com/spark/vllm">Spark playbook</a> the container.',
