    'install.chip.remote': 'Connects to Cedar on another computer',
    'install.ledeOld': 'Tell us about the computer, then pick how Cedar gets its model: from a provider, or from a server you run. The steps below follow your answers, and the page address remembers them.',
    'install.model.ledeOld': 'Cedar needs an AI model to think with. There are two ways to give it one.',
    'install.pick.addressOld': 'type the address <code>{address}</code>',
    'install.remote.linkTitle': 'Get the connection link from the other computer',
    'install.remote.linkBody': 'On the computer that runs Cedar, open the chat’s <strong>Settings → Phone</strong> and click <strong>Copy connection link</strong>. If Cedar runs there in the Mac or Windows app, its setup page has the same under <strong>iPhone, iPad & Android</strong>.',
    'install.remote.linkWhat': 'The link holds that computer’s address and its access token, so treat it like a password. You can also copy the address and the token one by one.',
    'install.remote.https': 'The address has to start with <code>https://</code>. Cedar gets such an address when it is shared over Tailscale (<code>https://&lt;computer&gt;.&lt;tailnet&gt;.ts.net</code>): in the Mac or Windows app, turn on <strong>Share with the phone apps over Tailscale</strong>; on Linux, follow <a href="{url}">the Linux guide</a>.',
    'install.remote.reachTitle': 'Put this computer on the same Tailscale network',
    'install.remote.reachBody': 'A <code>ts.net</code> address answers only to your own devices. Install Tailscale on this computer and sign in with the account the other computer uses. Skip this step if this computer already reaches the address.',
    'install.remote.getTailscale': 'Get Tailscale',
    'install.remote.connectTitle': 'Connect Cedar to it',
    'install.remote.connect1': 'Open Cedar. When it asks <strong>How do you want to use Cedar?</strong>, choose <strong>Connect to Cedar on another computer</strong>.',
    'install.remote.connect2': 'Paste the connection link, or type the <strong>Server address</strong> and the <strong>Access token</strong>, and click <strong>Connect</strong>.',
    'install.remote.connect3': 'Cedar checks that the server answers and accepts the token, then restarts and shows its chat.',
    'install.remote.already': 'Cedar is already set up on this computer? Open <strong>Use Cedar running on another computer</strong> at the top of its setup page instead. More in the <a href="{url}">desktop guide</a>.',
    'install.remote.expect': '<b>What this means.</b> Conversations, agents and memory live on the other computer, and scheduled agents keep running there while this one sleeps. Its models and tools are set up in that chat’s Settings. <strong>Disconnect</strong> on the setup page goes back to running Cedar on this computer.',
    'install.remote.linuxTitle': 'Open it in a browser',
    'install.remote.linuxBody': 'Open the other computer’s address in a browser and enter the access token. It is the same chat the apps show.',
    'install.remote.linuxNote': 'There is no ready-made Cedar app for Linux; it can be <a href="{url}">built from source</a>.',
    'install.remote.phoneTitle': 'Connect your phone to it too',
    'install.remote.phoneScan': 'On the other computer, open the chat’s <strong>Settings → Phone</strong> and scan the QR code with the Cedar app (Settings → <strong>Scan QR Code</strong>).',
